{"bookId":"69048808ef55966cf1d71f1d","moduleId":"69075c9549e6141a77a5929e","subjectId":"69075cb049e6141a77a59709","chapterId":"69075cb149e6141a77a59713","subject":"IOQM","chapter":"Sets and Relations","count":1,"questions":[{"id":314792,"subject":"IOQM","chapter":"Sets and Relations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Olympiad workbook","q":"Let $A$ and $B$ be two finite sets such that there are exactly 144 sets which are subsets of $A$ or subsets of $B$. Find the number of elements in $A \\cup B$.","options":[],"answer":"08","solution":"<img width=200px src=\"https://cdn-question-pool..app/NEET/Olympiad/sqv2vAoTnf-eyXJ97CwTwzYNOagrmMo-jb1vBax5A2c.original.fullsize.png\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-3391df8af35c3423.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-3391df8af35c3423.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & 2^{a+b}+2^{b+c}-2^b=144=2^4 \\cdot 9 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & 2^b\\left(2^a+2^c-1\\right)=2^4 \\cdot 9 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & b=4 \\& a=1, c=3 \\\\ & n(A \\cup B)=5+7-4=8\\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Olympiad workbook","_book":"69048808ef55966cf1d71f1d","_chapterKey":"69048808ef55966cf1d71f1d__69075c9549e6141a77a5929e__69075cb049e6141a77a59709__69075cb149e6141a77a59713","_marksId":"69075c9649e6141a77a592b5","type":"numerical","questionType":"numerical","correctValue":"08"}]}